<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44330" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simplus</span></b> , a, um. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj.
			kindr. with simplex, <i>simple;</i> as
				adj. only post-class.: mors, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 878.—More freq.,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simplum</span></b> , i,
				n., <i>that which is single</i> or <i>simple</i>, <i>the simple sum</i> or
				<i>number</i> (opp. to the double): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duplum simplum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Top. 11, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simplum solvere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 5, 6, 25</span></i>
			 (opp. duplum, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 6,
			14</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si simplum imperetur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					29, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 49, 14,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simpla</span></b> , ae,
				f. (sc. pecunia), <i>the simple
				purchase-money</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 2, 10, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 21,
				2, 60</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
